    "source": "public:NVD_fix_pattern",
    "verified": "runtime_gate_passed",
    "notes": "CVE-2022-1285: webhook delivery did not re-check that the payload URL resolves outside local networks (creation-time check only, and API creation has no check at all). Fixed in 0.12.8/0.12.9 by checking at delivery time. Residual: delivery still follows HTTP redirects (Go http.Client default), so an allowlisted/attacker-controlled receiver can redirect the signed payload to an internal address -> CVE-2026-47267, fixed 0.14.3 by refusing all redirects. PoC: admin creates webhook via API (bypasses UI localCIDR validation), triggers 'Test Delivery', reads the delivery record where the redirected internal canary response body is rendered. attacker service (host port 33690) 302-redirects to canary; canary is internal-only. v1/v2 app.ini gets [security] LOCAL_NETWORK_ALLOWLIST = attacker so the attacker URL passes the delivery-time check. Built 2026-08-01.",
